{"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"IDs an app has declared it is editing, exempt from a re-hydration merge for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as long as the hold is in force.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/init()"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/ids","doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/isEmpty"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/hold(_:)","doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/isHolding(_:)","doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/release(_:)","doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/releaseAll()"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@"},{"kind":"attribute","text":"MainActor","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"final"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EditingHolds"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every other exemption is inferred: ","type":"text"},{"code":"Swidux\/EntityStore\/changes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writer’s drained-but-unflushed buffers, and the failed-flush ledger all","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"describe writes the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"store","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" has seen. A value still sitting in a view’s local","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is in none of them, so under","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy\/preferRemote","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" a remote edit can land underneath a half-typed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"field and the user’s next keystroke dispatches against a value that changed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out from under them.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A hold closes exactly that window, and nothing wider:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["TextEditor(text: $draft)","    .holdsEntity(note.id, in: persistence.editing)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Prefer that modifier — it takes the hold when the editor appears and gives it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"back when the editor goes away, so there is no release to forget. Reach for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/hold(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/release(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" directly only where the editing session","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"isn’t a view’s lifetime.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"What a hold is not","type":"heading","anchor":"What-a-hold-is-not","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A hold ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"defers a remote change; it does not veto one.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Release it and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"next merge applies whatever storage holds, including a deletion made","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elsewhere. The worst a leaked hold can do is strand one row at a stale","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value, which is what ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy\/preferInMemory","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" does on purpose. It is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not data loss, and it is not silent either: a merge that actually withheld a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"differing value reports","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceDiagnostic\/mergeWithheld(entityType:ids:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two alternatives cost less and are often enough. ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.binding(_:sending:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dispatches on write, which makes the value a drained-but-unflushed one and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers it already. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy\/preferInMemory","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" exempts a whole collection","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"permanently. A hold sits between them: remote-wins stays on everywhere else,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and here only while the user is actually typing.","type":"text"}]}